% Demo: subscription_billing_before_python.prompt
%
% This is the BEFORE state — a realistic billing-service prompt with
% common ambiguity problems that the prompt repair feature detects and fixes.
%
% Run to see all issues:
%   pdd checkup lint demos/prompt_repair/subscription_billing_before_python.prompt
%
% Run to repair automatically:
%   pdd checkup demos/prompt_repair/subscription_billing_before_python.prompt --prompt-repair best-effort
%
% Expected: 6 VAGUE_TERM warnings before repair, 0 after.

<contract_rules>
R1 - Subscription renewal
The system MUST process renewals for all active subscriptions due within the billing window.

R2 - Payment processing
The system MUST charge the valid payment method on file and record a billing receipt.

R3 - Failure handling
The system MUST handle failed payments gracefully and apply reasonable retry logic.

R4 - Customer notification
The system MUST notify the customer on successful billing within 5 minutes.

R5 - Idempotency
The system MUST NOT double-charge any subscription within the same billing cycle.
</contract_rules>

<requirements>
- Process monthly and annual subscriptions.
- Support USD, EUR, and GBP currencies.
- Write structured audit logs for every billing attempt.
- Expose idempotency_key on all charge requests.
</requirements>
